      <Row><!--1182-->
         <Value ColumnRef="ModelName">
            <SimpleValue>UBL-CommonLibrary-2.5</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="ComponentName">
            <SimpleValue>PreferenceCriterionCode</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="Cardinality">
            <SimpleValue>0..1</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="Definition">
            <SimpleValue>A code signifying the treatment preference for this goods item according to international trading agreements.</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="Examples">
            <SimpleValue>Preference Criterion is used in the following manner in the paper CO of another country (e.g.): A - The good is wholly obtained or produced entirely in the territory of one or more of the NAFTA countries as reference in Article 415. Note: The purchase of a good in the territory does not necessarily render it wholly obtained or produced . If the good is an agricultural good, see also criterion F and Annex 703.2. (Reference: Article 401(a), 415). B - ... C - ... D - ... E - ... F - The good is an originating agricultural good under preference criterion A,B, or C above and is not subjected to quantitative restriction in the importing NAFTA country because.... Thus, the column Preference Criterion will indicate either A, B, C,...</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="DictionaryEntryName">
            <SimpleValue>Goods Item. Preference Criterion Code. Code</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="ObjectClass">
            <SimpleValue>Goods Item</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="PropertyTermPossessiveNoun">
            <SimpleValue>Preference Criterion</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="PropertyTermPrimaryNoun">
            <SimpleValue>Code</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="PropertyTerm">
            <SimpleValue>Preference Criterion Code</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="RepresentationTerm">
            <SimpleValue>Code</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="DataType">
            <SimpleValue>Code. Type</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="ComponentType">
            <SimpleValue>BBIE</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="UNTDEDCode">
            <SimpleValue>9285</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="CurrentVersion">
            <SimpleValue>2.0</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
         <Value ColumnRef="EditorsNotes">
            <SimpleValue>Change for UBL 2.0 Update Package: Cell G424 changed from Criterion to Code ; cell F424 changed from Preference to Preference Criterion</SimpleValue>
         </Value>
      </Row>
